onumber \ &=& \int_{[0,1]^{d-1}} \ensuremath{\mathbb{P}}(\{x\}	imes [0,1] \subset \ensuremath{D_{	ext{fat}}}) d\lambda_{d-1} >0. \end{eqnarray*} Hence,  egin{equation} \lambda_{d-1}(\{x\in [0,1]^{d-1} : \{x\}	imes [0,1] \subset \ensuremath{D_{	ext{fat}}} \}) > 0 \end{equation} with positive probability. Observe that \[ \ensuremath{D_{	ext{fat}}^{c}} \supset  igcup_{x \in [0,1]^{d-1}: \{x\}	imes[0,1]\subset \ensuremath{D_{	ext{fat}}}} \{x\} 	imes [0,1]. \] In particular, \[ \lambda(\ensuremath{D_{	ext{fat}}^{c}}) \geq \lambda_{d-1}(\{x\in [0,1]^{d-1} : \{x\}	imes [0,1] \subset \ensuremath{D_{	ext{fat}}}\}). \] From \eqref{strictly positive} we conclude that $\lambda(\ensuremath{D_{	ext{fat}}^{c}})>0$ with positive probability. It now follows from Theorem ef{thm lebesgue} that the Lebesgue measure of the dust set is 0 a.s. (iii) Next assume that $\prod_{n=1}^{\infty} p_n^{N^{dn}} > 0$. For each level $n$, we have $\ensuremath{\mathbb{P}}(\ensuremath{D_{	ext{fat}}}^n=\ensuremath{D_{	ext{fat}}}^{n-1}) \geq p_n^{N^{dn}}$. Since $\prod_{n=1}^{\infty} p_n^{N^{dn}} > 0$ is equivalent to $\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}( 1 - p_n^{N^{dn}}) < \infty$, we have \[ \sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \ensuremath{\mathbb{P}}(\ensuremath{D_{	ext{fat}}}^n
eq \ensuremath{D_{	ext{fat}}}^{n-1}) \leq \sum_{n=1}^{\infty} (1 - p_n^{N^{dn}}) < \infty. \] Applying the Borel-Cantelli lemma gives that, with probability 1, $\{\ensuremath{D_{	ext{fat}}}^n 
eq \ensuremath{D_{	ext{fat}}}^{n-1}\}$ occurs for only finitely many $n$. Hence, with probability 1 there exists an $n$ such that $\ensuremath{D_{	ext{fat}}}$ can be written as the union of level-$n$ cubes.

